---
title: Hand-torn Cabbage (Shou Si Bao Cai 手撕包菜)
description: A spicy, sour, and savory stir-fry. Tearing the cabbage by hand creates irregular edges that absorb more flavor than chopping.
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 5 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - cabbage
  - vegetable
  - spicy
  - chinese
  - side
cuisine: Chinese
course: Side
---

> Tearing the cabbage instead of cutting it with a knife helps it absorb the sauce better. Don't skip the pork belly if you want the authentic flavor, though it can be omitted for a vegetarian version.

== Prepare Ingredients ==

Remove the core from the @green cabbage{½%head}. Tear the leaves into irregular bite-sized pieces, discarding any thick, tough ribs. Wash and drain very well.

Slice the @pork belly{50%g} into thin strips.
Slice the @garlic{3%cloves}.
Cut the @dried chilies{4%whole} into halves, shaking out the seeds if you prefer less heat.

== Sauce Mix ==

In a small #bowl{}, combine:
- @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}
- @black vinegar{1%tbsp}
- @sugar{½%tsp}
- @salt{¼%tsp}

== Stir-fry ==

Heat a #wok{} over medium heat. Add @neutral oil{1%tbsp} and the sliced pork belly. Cook until the pork releases its fat and turns slightly crispy.

Add the sliced garlic, dried chilies, and @Sichuan peppercorns{1%tsp}. Stir-fry for ~{15%seconds} until fragrant.

Turn the heat up to high. Add the torn cabbage leaves. Stir-fry constantly for ~{2%minutes} until the leaves soften and start to slightly char at the edges.

== Finish ==

Pour the sauce mixture over the cabbage. Toss vigorously for another ~{1%minute} until the cabbage is well coated and the sauce is mostly absorbed or evaporated.

Serve hot.